<main id="main">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Procurement evidence</span><h1>A transparent evidence map for evaluators and bid reviewers.</h1><p>This page makes a clear distinction between verified company information, founder portfolio evidence, proposed delivery arrangements and items that must be supported separately in the tender submission.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container">
<div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">Evidence classes</span><h2>What this website demonstrates.</h2></div><p>Website content is supporting evidence only; it does not replace the tender response, portal declarations, certificates, insurance schedules, financial information or contractual documents.</p></div>
<div class="grid-2">
<article class="card"><div class="icon">01</div><h3>Verified company facts</h3><p>Company name, company number, registered office, active status, incorporation date and SIC classifications are presented consistently across the site based on the company details supplied for this build.</p><div class="pill-row"><span class="pill">About</span><span class="pill">Footer</span><span class="pill">Contact</span></div></article>
<article class="card"><div class="icon">02</div><h3>Founder portfolio evidence</h3><p>Technical capability is illustrated through work carried on from the existing public portfolio, including software, data science, machine learning and application development. These are not represented as previous commercial contracts of this company.</p><div class="pill-row"><span class="pill">Technical Work</span><span class="pill">Projects</span></div></article>
<article class="card"><div class="icon">03</div><h3>Proposed delivery capability</h3><p>The site describes a practical delivery model for digital mapping, data, software and business-support work. Proposed roles are separated from proven employee evidence so the bid can be updated with confirmed personnel.</p><div class="pill-row"><span class="pill">Services</span><span class="pill">Team</span></div></article>
<article class="card"><div class="icon">04</div><h3>Operating controls</h3><p>Accessibility, information security, data protection, QA, change control and continuity principles are stated as operating practices rather than third-party certifications.</p><div class="pill-row"><span class="pill">Controls</span><span class="pill">Policies</span></div></article>
</div></div></section>
<section class="section soft"><div class="container">
<div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">Bid-readiness matrix</span><h2>Evidence still to be attached or verified.</h2></div></div>
<div class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><thead><tr><th>Evidence item</th><th>Website treatment</th><th>Bid evidence needed</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Legal entity information</td><td>Company identity and registered office are repeated consistently.</td><td>Official Companies House extract or other buyer-requested corporate evidence.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Named delivery staff</td><td>Nine-role proposed structure is shown and marked illustrative.</td><td>Replace placeholders with confirmed names, responsibilities and CVs before submission.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Relevant experience</td><td>Existing portfolio work is shown as technical/founder evidence.</td><td>Use only references and case studies that can be evidenced as commercial contracts or otherwise accepted by the tender.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Insurance</td><td>No unsupported limits or policies are claimed.</td><td>Upload current certificates and limits required by the procurement documents.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Financial standing</td><td>No invented turnover or financial metrics are shown.</td><td>Provide declarations, accounts or other tests required by the tender pack.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Cyber / data protection assurance</td><td>Practical controls are described.</td><td>Provide formal policies, agreements, assessments, certifications or questionnaires where requested.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Detailed technical response</td><td>Digital map architecture and UX approach are described at a high level.</td><td>Complete the formal method statement against every scored requirement in the tender documents.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Price / commercial offer</td><td>Not published on the public website.</td><td>Submit through the procurement portal in the buyer's required format.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
</div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="route-card card"><div><h3>Submission principle</h3><span>Every substantive claim in the bid should be traceable to a company record, confirmed CV, portfolio source, contract reference, policy, certificate or other documentary evidence.</span></div><a class="btn btn-primary" href="tender-alignment.html">Review tender alignment</a></div></div></section>
</main>
